task.action:
- Create apps/festinalente/src/cli/types.ts with:
  - CliCommand interface (name, description, schema, handler)
  - CliResult type (tagged union: SuccessResult | ErrorResult)
  - Zod schemas for common CLI args (id, keywords, flags)
  - Branded types: TaskId, QuickId, DocId
- Create apps/festinalente/src/cli/registry.ts with:
  - CommandRegistry type (Map of command name to CliCommand)
  - registerCommand factory function
  - getCommand lookup function
  - listCommands function for --help

Types should follow tagged-union-errors pattern:
```typescript
interface SuccessResult<T> {
  readonly success: true;
  readonly data: T;
}
interface ErrorResult {
  readonly error: true;
  readonly message: string;
}
type CliResult<T> = SuccessResult<T> | ErrorResult;
```

- Create task.handler.ts:
  - createTaskHandler(deps) factory injecting fs capability and xml computer
  - Handlers: findTask, listTasks, deleteTask, nextId
  - Each handler validates args with zod, returns CliResult
  - Migrate logic from: find-task.ts, list-tasks.ts, delete-task.ts, next-id.ts

- Create spec.handler.ts:
  - createSpecHandler(deps) factory
  - Handlers: findSpec, findPlan
  - Migrate logic from: find-spec.ts, find-plan.ts

- Create quick.handler.ts:
  - createQuickHandler(deps) factory
  - Handlers: findQuick, nextQuickId
  - Migrate logic from: find-quick.ts, next-quick-id.ts

Handler pattern:
```typescript
export function createTaskHandler(deps: TaskHandlerDeps) {
  const findTask = (args: string[]): CliResult<TaskInfo> => {
    const parsed = findTaskSchema.safeParse({ id: args[0] });
    if (!parsed.success) {
      return { error: true, message: parsed.error.message };
    }
    // ... implementation
  };
  return { findTask, listTasks, deleteTask, nextId };
}
```

- Create cli.orchestrator.ts:
  - createCliOrchestrator(deps) factory
  - Register all commands from handlers into registry
  - Route incoming command to appropriate handler
  - Handle --help flag
  - Handle unknown commands with error + available commands list

- Create index.ts (composition root):
  - Parse process.argv
  - Create capabilities (fs, git)
  - Create computers (xml, yaml, search, validation)
  - Create handlers with injected deps
  - Create orchestrator with handlers
  - Execute command and output JSON

Orchestrator must be thin (~100 lines):
```typescript
export function createCliOrchestrator(deps: CliOrchestratorDeps) {
  const registry = createRegistry();

  // Register commands from each handler
  for (const [name, handler] of Object.entries(deps.taskHandler)) {
    registry.register(name, handler);
  }
  // ... register other handlers

  function execute(command: string, args: string[]): CliResult<unknown> {
    if (command === '--help') return listCommands(registry);
    const handler = registry.get(command);
    if (!handler) return { error: true, message: `Unknown command: ${command}` };
    return handler(args);
  }

  return { execute };
}
```

Entry point pattern:
```typescript
// index.ts - thin composition root
const fs = createFileSystemCapability();
const git = createGitCapability();
const xml = createXmlParserComputer();
// ... create all deps
const orchestrator = createCliOrchestrator({ taskHandler, searchHandler, ... });
const result = orchestrator.execute(command, args);
console.log(JSON.stringify(result, null, 2));
process.exit(result.error ? 1 : 0);
```
